msgid "资源容量与 Linux ABI"
msgstr "Resource capacity and the Linux ABI"

msgid ""
"本章说明资源分配策略与已实现接口的边界，不表示 ReliefNT 已完整实现 Linux 或 "
"POSIX。内存耗尽、资源配额和硬件地址范围仍会限制资源数量。"
msgstr ""
"This chapter explains resource-allocation policies and the boundaries of "
"implemented interfaces; it does not imply that ReliefNT fully implements "
"Linux or POSIX. Memory exhaustion, resource quotas, and hardware address "
"ranges still limit resource counts."

msgid ""
"``/proc/PID/oom_score`` 使用独立的 Linux 6.12 风格 0..2000 展示值， 不改变内部 OOM 选择策略。RSS "
"只计入有实际 RAM 后备的用户页面，另计 swap 槽引用，不把设备 PFN 当作 RAM。``oom_score_adj`` 的读取和写入先 "
"经过普通 proc DAC 与 PID 身份检查；降低到继承的下限以下需要 ``CAP_SYS_RESOURCE``。进程退出后保留的 proc "
"身份不会指向重用的 PID。"
msgstr ""
"``/proc/PID/oom_score`` uses a separate Linux 6.12-style display value of "
"0..2000 without changing the internal OOM selection policy. RSS counts only "
"user pages with actual RAM backing, with swap-slot references counted "
"separately; device PFNs are not treated as RAM. Reads and writes of "
"``oom_score_adj`` first pass ordinary proc DAC and PID identity checks; "
"lowering it below the inherited floor requires ``CAP_SYS_RESOURCE``. A proc "
"identity retained after process exit does not point to a reused PID."

msgid "容量与生命周期"
msgstr "Capacity and lifecycles"

msgid ""
"``getrlimit``、``setrlimit`` 和 ``prlimit64`` 支持进程共享的 "
"``RLIMIT_FSIZE``，新进程默认软、硬限制均为 unlimited，并沿 fork/exec "
"继承。普通文件写入在边界处返回合法短写；从边界及其之后继续写入时返回 ``EFBIG`` 并发送 "
"``SIGXFSZ``。截断和会增长文件的预分配在写入前检查 新大小，``FALLOC_FL_KEEP_SIZE`` "
"不因预分配范围超出限制而改变逻辑大小。 文件复制与 memfd/shmem 写入也受该限制；设备、管道和生成的 proc/sysfs "
"控制文件不套用普通文件大小配额。OpenSSH 的预认证沙箱可以将此限制降为 零，不会因此获得不受限制的文件写入能力。"
msgstr ""
"``getrlimit``, ``setrlimit``, and ``prlimit64`` support process-shared "
"``RLIMIT_FSIZE``. New processes default to unlimited soft and hard limits, "
"inherited through fork/exec. Regular-file writes return valid short writes "
"at the boundary; further writes at or beyond it return ``EFBIG`` and send "
"``SIGXFSZ``. Truncation and preallocation that grows a file check the new "
"size before writing; ``FALLOC_FL_KEEP_SIZE`` does not change logical size "
"when the preallocated range exceeds the limit. File copying and memfd/shmem "
"writes are also subject to this limit; devices, pipes, and generated "
"proc/sysfs control files do not use regular-file size quotas. OpenSSH's pre-"
"authentication sandbox can lower this limit to zero without thereby "
"acquiring unrestricted file-writing ability."

msgid ""
"任务枚举直接遍历调度器的任务表。``/proc`` 的进程列表、线程统计以及 memfd 的可写共享映射检查不截断为前 64 "
"个任务。描述符目录使用实际文件表 和 PTY 别名，不截断为前 1024 个描述符。"
msgstr ""
"Task enumeration walks the scheduler's task table directly. Process lists "
"and thread statistics in ``/proc``, and memfd writable-shared-mapping "
"checks, are not truncated to the first 64 tasks. Descriptor directories use "
"the actual file table and PTY aliases, without truncation to the first 1024 "
"descriptors."

msgid ""
"内部对象注册表按需扩容，扩容不移动对象，分配在自旋锁外完成。句柄保留 16 位槽号和 16 位代际编码，最多表示 65535 个同时存在的槽；此编码上限"
" 仍然存在。查找句柄只返回借用引用，调用方必须按所属子系统的锁和引用规则 保证对象存活。"
msgstr ""
"Internal object registries grow on demand without moving objects, and "
"allocation happens outside spinlocks. Handles retain a 16-bit slot number "
"and 16-bit generation encoding, representing at most 65535 simultaneous "
"slots; this encoding limit remains. Handle lookup returns only a borrowed "
"reference, and callers must preserve object lifetime under the owning "
"subsystem's locking and reference rules."

msgid "等待队列使用任务内嵌链表节点。IRQ 唤醒不分配内存；任务退出和取消等待 必须先脱链。队列本身的存储必须活到所有等待者脱离后才能释放。"
msgstr ""
"Wait queues use list nodes embedded in tasks. IRQ wakeup allocates no "
"memory; task exit and wait cancellation must first unlink the node. Queue "
"storage itself must remain alive until all waiters have detached."

msgid ""
"epoll 监听表按需扩容；注册键由描述符编号和打开文件描述共同确定。 关闭一个编号后，``dup``、``fork``、排队中的 "
"``SCM_RIGHTS`` 或在途 I/O 引用仍可维持原对象的监听；重新使用该编号不会把旧监听转向新对象。 "
"监听项只借用稳定的对象身份，最终引用释放时反向清除监听，不延长对象生命周期。 当前不支持嵌套 epoll，向 epoll 实例注册另一个 epoll "
"实例时返回 ``EPERM``； 直接 ``poll`` epoll 描述符只查看已就绪的监听项，不消费 ET/ONESHOT 状态。 原始 "
"``select``/``pselect6`` 系统调用按 ``nfds`` 复制位图，并检查 "
"``RLIMIT_NOFILE``、溢出、无效描述符和用户指针。libc 的 ``fd_set`` 大小 由 libc 决定，不能用 "
"``FD_SET`` 操作其表示范围以外的描述符。"
msgstr ""
"epoll watch tables grow on demand; registration keys combine the descriptor "
"number and open file description. After a number is closed, ``dup``, "
"``fork``, queued ``SCM_RIGHTS``, or in-flight I/O references can keep the "
"original object's watch alive; reusing the number does not redirect the old "
"watch to a new object. Watch entries only borrow a stable object identity "
"and are removed through reverse cleanup when the final reference is "
"released, without extending object lifetime. Nested epoll is currently "
"unsupported; registering another epoll instance with an epoll instance "
"returns ``EPERM``. Directly using ``poll`` on an epoll descriptor only "
"inspects ready watches without consuming ET/ONESHOT state. Raw "
"``select``/``pselect6`` syscalls copy bitmaps according to ``nfds`` and "
"check ``RLIMIT_NOFILE``, overflow, invalid descriptors, and user pointers. "
"libc determines its ``fd_set`` size; ``FD_SET`` must not be used on "
"descriptors beyond its representable range."

msgid "管道"
msgstr "Pipes"

msgid ""
"管道对象与环形缓冲区分别分配，不再使用固定 256 项全局池。 ``PIPE_BUF`` 保持 4096 字节；不超过此值的非阻塞写入具有全写或 "
"``EAGAIN`` 的原子语义，较大写入允许短写。"
msgstr ""
"Pipe objects and ring buffers are allocated separately, replacing the fixed "
"global pool of 256 entries. ``PIPE_BUF`` remains 4096 bytes; nonblocking "
"writes no larger than this have all-or-``EAGAIN`` atomic semantics, while "
"larger writes may be short."

msgid ""
"命名管道按解析后的 inode 类型进入管道实现，不从权限位推断文件类型。 没有对端时，阻塞打开等待另一端；非阻塞写端打开返回 ``ENXIO``。 "
"``O_PATH`` 只保留路径，不参与对端会合。原生探针 ``tools/tests/fifo_abi_test.c`` "
"检查磁盘和内存文件系统上的数据、断开通知、 信号中断及打开等待；可通过命令行指定测试目录。"
msgstr ""
"Named pipes enter the pipe implementation according to the resolved inode "
"type, without inferring file type from permission bits. With no peer, a "
"blocking open waits for the other end; a nonblocking write-end open returns "
"``ENXIO``. ``O_PATH`` retains only the path and does not participate in "
"endpoint rendezvous. The native probe ``tools/tests/fifo_abi_test.c`` checks"
" data, disconnect notifications, signal interruption, and open waits on disk"
" and memory filesystems; the test directory can be specified on the command "
"line."

msgid ""
"``F_GETPIPE_SZ`` 查询可用容量；``F_SETPIPE_SZ`` 向上取整到至少一页的 二次幂容量。缩小到不足以容纳现有数据时返回 "
"``EBUSY``，失败不改变数据 顺序或容量。"
msgstr ""
"``F_GETPIPE_SZ`` queries usable capacity; ``F_SETPIPE_SZ`` rounds up to a "
"power-of-two capacity of at least one page. Shrinking below the size needed "
"for existing data returns ``EBUSY``; failure leaves data order and capacity "
"unchanged."

msgid ""
"默认容量为 16 页。当前每个 UID 的软预算为 16384 页；达到预算后，新建 管道使用两页。无资源管理能力的调用者不能把单管道扩大到 1 MiB"
" 以上， 也不能通过扩容超出软预算。``CAP_SYS_RESOURCE`` 或 ``CAP_SYS_ADMIN`` "
"可绕过这项资源策略；分配失败仍会返回错误。这些是内核策略常量，当前未 通过 sysctl 暴露，不能将其误称为已支持 Linux 的全部管道 "
"sysctl。"
msgstr ""
"Default capacity is 16 pages. The current per-UID soft budget is 16384 "
"pages; once reached, new pipes use two pages. Callers without resource-"
"management capabilities cannot grow a single pipe beyond 1 MiB or exceed the"
" soft budget by growing pipes. ``CAP_SYS_RESOURCE`` or ``CAP_SYS_ADMIN`` can"
" bypass this resource policy; allocation failures still return errors. These"
" are kernel policy constants and are not currently exposed through sysctl; "
"they must not be described as support for all Linux pipe sysctls."

msgid ""
"参考：`pipe(7) <https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/pipe.7.html>`_ 和 "
"`F_GETPIPE_SZ(2const) <https://man7.org/linux/man-"
"pages/man2/F_GETPIPE_SZ.2const.html>`_。"
msgstr ""
"References: `pipe(7) <https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/pipe.7.html>`_ "
"and `F_GETPIPE_SZ(2const) <https://man7.org/linux/man-"
"pages/man2/F_GETPIPE_SZ.2const.html>`_."

msgid "匿名共享文件"
msgstr "Anonymous shared files"

msgid ""
"memfd 使用不挂载的内部 tmpfs 实例。它不占用用户挂载卷槽，也不需要一个 与文件逻辑大小相同的连续物理内存块。逻辑扩展是稀疏的，实际页面按访问"
" 分配，空洞读为零；不再使用 32 项专用池或桌面分辨率作为文件大小上限。"
msgstr ""
"memfd uses an unmounted internal tmpfs instance. It consumes no user mount-"
"volume slot and does not require a contiguous physical-memory block as large"
" as the logical file size. Logical expansion is sparse, actual pages are "
"allocated on access, and holes read as zero; the old dedicated pool of 32 "
"entries and desktop resolution no longer limit file size."

msgid ""
"打开文件描述与 VMA 各自持有 inode 引用，关闭最后一个描述符不会提前释放 仍被映射的页面。``MAP_SHARED`` "
"保持别名一致性，``MAP_PRIVATE`` 使用 COW。 缩小文件先撤销受影响映射，再释放页面，重新扩展不能暴露旧数据。"
msgstr ""
"Open file descriptions and VMAs each hold inode references, so closing the "
"last descriptor does not prematurely release pages that remain mapped. "
"``MAP_SHARED`` preserves alias consistency, while ``MAP_PRIVATE`` uses COW. "
"Shrinking first revokes affected mappings before freeing pages, so "
"subsequent expansion cannot expose old data."

msgid ""
"seal 状态随共享文件描述持有。增加 ``F_SEAL_WRITE`` 时检查所有任务中可能 写入的共享 VMA，存在这类映射时返回 "
"``EBUSY``；私有 COW 映射不阻止封印。 封印后的新共享映射不能借助后续 ``mprotect`` 绕过写保护。"
msgstr ""
"Seal state is held with the shared file description. Adding ``F_SEAL_WRITE``"
" checks potentially writable shared VMAs across all tasks and returns "
"``EBUSY`` if any exist; private COW mappings do not prevent sealing. New "
"shared mappings after sealing cannot bypass write protection through later "
"``mprotect`` calls."

msgid ""
"参考：`memfd_create(2) <https://man7.org/linux/man-"
"pages/man2/memfd_create.2.html>`_ 和 `F_GET_SEALS(2const) "
"<https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/F_GET_SEALS.2const.html>`_。"
msgstr ""
"References: `memfd_create(2) <https://man7.org/linux/man-"
"pages/man2/memfd_create.2.html>`_ and `F_GET_SEALS(2const) "
"<https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/F_GET_SEALS.2const.html>`_."

msgid "终端与网络"
msgstr "Terminals and networking"

msgid ""
"PTY 会话分块分配并保持稳定标识，任务的 PTY 描述符表按需扩容。 ``dup``、``fork``、描述符传递和关闭仍遵守端点引用与 "
"``RLIMIT_NOFILE``。六个虚拟控制台属于显示配置，不等于用户 PTY 数量上限。"
msgstr ""
"PTY sessions are allocated in chunks with stable identifiers, and tasks' PTY"
" descriptor tables grow on demand. ``dup``, ``fork``, descriptor passing, "
"and close still obey endpoint references and ``RLIMIT_NOFILE``. The six "
"virtual consoles are a display configuration, not a limit on user PTYs."

msgid ""
"UNIX、UDP、TCP 套接字注册表与 UNIX 监听队列按需分配。旧控制接口中的 定长连接快照只限制一次快照的展示数量，不限制实际存活连接数量。 "
"单连接收发缓冲区仍有界，缓冲区不足按阻塞或非阻塞语义处理。"
msgstr ""
"UNIX, UDP, and TCP socket registries and UNIX listen queues are allocated on"
" demand. Fixed-size connection snapshots in the old control interface limit "
"only the number shown in one snapshot, not the number of live connections. "
"Per-connection receive/transmit buffers remain bounded; buffer shortages "
"follow blocking or nonblocking semantics."

msgid ""
"TCP 写入先排队，ACK 与重传由网络服务推进，阻塞调用经调度器停车。 非阻塞调用返回进展、短写或 ``EAGAIN``，不能等待远端 ACK。 本地"
" FIN 占用一个序列号并跟踪 ACK、RTO 重试和最终协议失败；FIN 未确认时 套接字不会被回收。本地写半关闭后仍可读取对端数据；收到对端 FIN"
" 后读完 缓冲区才返回 EOF，本地发送方向仍可发送回复。``POLLRDHUP`` 表示对端 关闭发送方向，单向关闭不产生 "
"``POLLHUP``；双方关闭或连接终止才产生 HUP。 ``SO_SNDTIMEO``、``SO_RCVTIMEO`` "
"默认零表示无调用超时；协议重传耗尽 仍可能使连接失败。旧专用网络控制请求的显式毫秒超时与标准 socket 调用 分别处理。正超时向上取整到调度 "
"tick；Linux 兼容的负 ``tv_sec`` 表示 立即超时，查询仍归一为零值，与设置全零表示无限等待的行为不同。"
msgstr ""
"TCP writes are queued first, with ACKs and retransmission advanced by "
"network service, and blocking calls parked through the scheduler. "
"Nonblocking calls return progress, short writes, or ``EAGAIN`` and must not "
"wait for remote ACKs. A local FIN consumes one sequence number and tracks "
"ACK, RTO retries, and final protocol failure; the socket is not reclaimed "
"while FIN is unacknowledged. After local write-half shutdown, peer data can "
"still be read; after receiving a peer FIN, reads return EOF only after "
"draining the buffer, while the local send direction can still send replies. "
"``POLLRDHUP`` means the peer closed its send direction; a one-way shutdown "
"does not produce ``POLLHUP``. HUP occurs only when both sides close or the "
"connection terminates. ``SO_SNDTIMEO`` and ``SO_RCVTIMEO`` default to zero, "
"meaning no call timeout; protocol retransmission exhaustion can still fail "
"the connection. Explicit millisecond timeouts for legacy private network-"
"control requests are handled separately from standard socket calls. Positive"
" timeouts are rounded up to scheduler ticks; a Linux-compatible negative "
"``tv_sec`` means immediate timeout, though queries normalize it to zero, "
"unlike setting all zeros for an infinite wait."

msgid ""
"系统调用入口、用户态定时器返回和空闲服务路径在执行事务内推进有待处理的 TCP 工作；硬件 IRQ 中不执行会分配内存的网络处理。单次维护预算有界， "
"空队列不扫描所有套接字。最后一个描述符关闭或进程退出后，已接受但尚未 确认的数据仍由网络栈持有并继续发送。"
msgstr ""
"Syscall entry, userspace timer returns, and idle service paths advance "
"pending TCP work within execution transactions; hardware IRQs do not run "
"network processing that allocates memory. Each maintenance pass has a "
"bounded budget, and empty queues do not scan all sockets. After the last "
"descriptor is closed or the process exits, accepted but unacknowledged data "
"remains owned by the network stack and continues to be transmitted."

msgid ""
"这些改动不等同于完整 TCP 标准实现。当前保留旧控制接口的连接状态编号， 完整关闭状态及 2MSL 策略、RTT 自适应 "
"RTO、SACK、快速重传和窗口缩放仍 未实现；旧 DNS 和专用同步连接路径仍存在有界轮询。"
msgstr ""
"These changes do not amount to a complete TCP standards implementation. The "
"old control interface's connection-state numbers remain; complete close "
"states and a 2MSL policy, RTT-adaptive RTO, SACK, fast retransmit, and "
"window scaling are still unimplemented. Old DNS and private synchronous "
"connection paths still use bounded polling."

msgid ""
"参考：`epoll(7) <https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/epoll.7.html>`_、 `RFC "
"9293 <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9293.html>`_ 和 `RFC 6298 "
"<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6298.html>`_。"
msgstr ""
"References: `epoll(7) <https://man7.org/linux/man-"
"pages/man7/epoll.7.html>`_, `RFC 9293 <https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9293.html>`_, and `RFC 6298 <https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc6298.html>`_."

msgid "地址空间与驱动"
msgstr "Address spaces and drivers"

msgid ""
"用户页表按四级层次稀疏分配，支持低 canonical 半区，独占上界为 ``0x0000800000000000``。当前内核仍在低地址运行，保留 "
"``[0x08000000, 0x0c000000)`` 的 supervisor 区间；用户最小地址、堆区和 "
"栈增长窗口也仍有实现边界。这不是无条件可用的完整 128 TiB 连续区间。 ``RLIMIT_AS`` 和页权限检查继续有效。"
msgstr ""
"User page tables are allocated sparsely in four levels and support the lower"
" canonical half, with an exclusive upper bound of ``0x0000800000000000``. "
"The current kernel still runs at low addresses and reserves the supervisor "
"range ``[0x08000000, 0x0c000000)``; minimum user addresses, heap regions, "
"and stack-growth windows also retain implementation boundaries. This is not "
"an unconditionally available contiguous 128 TiB range. ``RLIMIT_AS`` and "
"page-permission checks still apply."

msgid ""
"普通匿名及文件 ``mmap``/``mprotect`` 按请求分别设置读、写和执行权限， 允许显式 ``PROT_WRITE | "
"PROT_EXEC``，以兼容 HotSpot 等 JIT 运行时。 没有请求执行权限的数据页保持 NX；再次移除 ``PROT_EXEC`` 会恢复 "
"NX。 懒分配、驻留匿名页及私有 COW 保持同一权限语义。文件访问模式、只读挂载、 ``noexec``、设备映射限制及 VMA 的 "
"``max_prot`` 上限继续生效，不能通过 后续 ``mprotect`` 增加被禁止的权限。"
msgstr ""
"Ordinary anonymous and file ``mmap``/``mprotect`` set read, write, and "
"execute permissions independently as requested, allowing explicit "
"``PROT_WRITE | PROT_EXEC`` for JIT runtimes such as HotSpot. Data pages "
"without requested execute permission remain NX; removing ``PROT_EXEC`` again"
" restores NX. Lazy allocation, resident anonymous pages, and private COW "
"retain the same permission semantics. File access modes, read-only mounts, "
"``noexec``, device-mapping restrictions, and the VMA's ``max_prot`` ceiling "
"remain effective; later ``mprotect`` cannot add prohibited permissions."

msgid ""
"这对应 Linux 默认权限组合行为，不表示已实现 Linux 的 MDWE/LSM 策略接口； SysV SHM 等独立接口的限制也不因此改变。参考 "
"`Linux 6.12 权限及 MDWE 规则 "
"<https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/include/linux/mman.h>`_。 "
"``tools/tests/jit_memory_runtime_probe.c`` 可在 Linux 和 ReliefOS 中运行， 检查 "
"W→WX、RWX 映射、撤销执行权限的 NX 效果及 fork COW 隔离。"
msgstr ""
"This follows Linux's default behavior for permission combinations and does "
"not imply implementation of Linux MDWE/LSM policy interfaces; restrictions "
"of separate interfaces such as SysV SHM are also unchanged. See `Linux 6.12 "
"permission and MDWE rules "
"<https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/include/linux/mman.h>`_. "
"``tools/tests/jit_memory_runtime_probe.c`` runs on Linux and ReliefOS to "
"check W→WX, RWX mappings, NX after revoking execute permission, and fork COW"
" isolation."

msgid ""
"跨核屏障和用户 TLB 刷新在内部串行发布请求，使请求代际与操作类型在 所有 CPU 确认前保持稳定。等待锁或确认的 CPU 即使关闭本地中断，也会 "
"处理其他 CPU 已发布的请求；返回时恢复调用前的中断状态。并行缺页中的 刷新也使用同一发布与确认路径。"
msgstr ""
"Cross-core barriers and user TLB flushes publish requests serially "
"internally, keeping the request generation and operation type stable until "
"all CPUs acknowledge. CPUs waiting for a lock or acknowledgment process "
"requests published by other CPUs even with local interrupts disabled, "
"restoring the pre-call interrupt state on return. Flushes during parallel "
"page faults use the same publication and acknowledgment path."

msgid ""
"懒加载 ELF 段只登记 VMA，较大的 BSS 不会提前分配覆盖全段的空页表。 实际访问时才建立页表和数据页。``fork`` "
"同时保护父子进程的私有可写页面， 写入后分别进行 COW；物理页引用计数超过 65535 仍保持完整所有权。 "
"计数达到最终表示上限时页面保持固定，避免未计入引用导致提前回收。"
msgstr ""
"Lazy-loaded ELF segments register only VMAs; large BSS regions do not "
"preallocate empty page tables for the entire segment. Page tables and data "
"pages are created only on actual access. ``fork`` protects private writable "
"pages in both parent and child, with separate COW on writes; physical-page "
"reference counts retain full ownership beyond 65535. Once the final "
"representational limit is reached, pages remain pinned to prevent uncounted "
"references from causing premature reclamation."

msgid ""
"内核访问物理页面使用 supervisor 直映射。当前 x86 PCI 后端采用直接 DMA， 设备描述符提交可寻址的物理地址，CPU 访问使用 "
"``mm_phys_to_virt`` 或驱动 API 回调；不能将两者混用。当前没有 IOMMU 或总线地址重映射实现，不能把 "
"总线地址与物理地址相同的假设推广到其他平台。 x86-64 内核直映射从 ``0xffff800000000000`` 开始，虚拟窗口为 64 TiB；"
" 可用物理地址还受 CPU 物理地址位数、可信固件拓扑、实际页表和可用元数据 约束。直映射稀疏建立，RAM 空洞不会因为落在窗口内而变成有效指针。 "
"物理类型、CPU 可表示性和页表实际覆盖是三个不同条件；分配器只接纳实际 映射的可信可用 RAM。引导期间页表仍需要在临时低地址映射内取得页面， "
"资源不足会使引导停止。64 TiB 是虚拟设计容量，不是已验证硬件 RAM 容量。"
msgstr ""
"The kernel accesses physical pages through a supervisor direct map. The "
"current x86 PCI backend uses direct DMA: device descriptors receive "
"addressable physical addresses, while CPU access uses ``mm_phys_to_virt`` or"
" driver API callbacks; the two must not be confused. There is currently no "
"IOMMU or bus-address remapping implementation, and equality of bus and "
"physical addresses must not be assumed on other platforms. The x86-64 kernel"
" direct map starts at ``0xffff800000000000`` with a 64 TiB virtual window; "
"usable physical addresses are further constrained by CPU physical-address "
"width, trusted firmware topology, actual page tables, and available "
"metadata. The direct map is built sparsely; RAM holes do not become valid "
"pointers merely because they fall within the window. Physical type, CPU "
"representability, and actual page-table coverage are three separate "
"conditions; the allocator accepts only actually mapped trusted usable RAM. "
"During boot, page tables still require pages obtained within temporary low-"
"address mappings; insufficient resources stop boot. 64 TiB is a virtual "
"design capacity, not a validated hardware RAM capacity."

msgid ""
"PCI BAR 可在 RAM 空洞内通过独立设备窗口映射；内核拒绝与 RAM 或已有 直映射别名冲突的缓存属性。DMA 使用设备实际地址掩码分配：例如 "
"DMA32 分配的最后一个字节也必须不超过 ``0xffffffff``。目前没有 IOMMU。 UEFI "
"若交接时启动服务仍活动，内核必须使用映像句柄和最新内存映射键 成功退出启动服务后才接管常规 RAM；无法证明所有权时停止引导。 "
"固件表发现还需证明当时的地址映射：活动 EFI amd64 入口的身份映射证明 可跨内核自己的退出启动服务调用保留；i386 入口只证明前 4 GiB。"
" 仅有已结束的 EFI 内存描述符不能证明高地址表当前可访问。"
msgstr ""
"PCI BARs in RAM holes can be mapped through a separate device window; the "
"kernel rejects cache attributes conflicting with RAM or existing direct-map "
"aliases. DMA allocation uses the device's actual address mask: for example, "
"even the final byte of a DMA32 allocation must not exceed ``0xffffffff``. "
"There is currently no IOMMU. If UEFI boot services are still active at "
"handoff, the kernel must successfully exit boot services using the image "
"handle and latest memory-map key before taking over ordinary RAM; boot stops"
" if ownership cannot be proven. Firmware-table discovery must also prove "
"address mappings at that time: identity-mapping evidence from an active EFI "
"amd64 entry can be retained across the kernel's own exit-boot-services call,"
" whereas an i386 entry proves only the first 4 GiB. EFI memory descriptors "
"from already-ended services alone do not prove that high-address tables are "
"currently accessible."

msgid ""
"内部驱动 API 版本为 2，末尾增加 ``phys_to_virt`` 回调。驱动必须检查 版本、``struct_size`` "
"和回调存在后才使用。版本 1 的驱动需要重新构建， 内核在初始化前拒绝不匹配的模块；Linux 系统调用 ABI 不因此改变。 "
"当前内置驱动随内核一起构建。"
msgstr ""
"The internal driver API is version 2, with a ``phys_to_virt`` callback "
"appended. Drivers must check the version, ``struct_size``, and callback "
"presence before use. Version 1 drivers need rebuilding, and the kernel "
"rejects mismatched modules before initialization; the Linux syscall ABI is "
"unchanged. Current built-in drivers are built together with the kernel."

msgid ""
"fbdev 的 ``smem_start`` 与用户设备映射的 PFN 保持物理地址语义，不能包含 内核直映射指针。显存与 FIFO "
"的物理保留范围也不能直接与 CPU 指针比较。 安装器根镜像的入口接收 Multiboot 模块物理地址，只在挂载实现内部转换。"
msgstr ""
"fbdev's ``smem_start`` and PFNs in user device mappings retain physical-"
"address semantics and must not contain kernel direct-map pointers. Physical "
"reservations for video memory and FIFO also must not be compared directly "
"with CPU pointers. The installer root-image entry receives physical "
"Multiboot module addresses and converts them only inside the mount "
"implementation."

msgid ""
"参考：`Linux DMA 地址说明 <https://docs.kernel.org/core-api/dma-api-howto.html#cpu-"
"and-dma-addresses>`_ 和 `Linux 6.12 fbdev UAPI "
"<https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/include/uapi/linux/fb.h>`_。"
msgstr ""
"References: `Linux DMA address explanation <https://docs.kernel.org/core-"
"api/dma-api-howto.html#cpu-and-dma-addresses>`_ and `Linux 6.12 fbdev UAPI "
"<https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/include/uapi/linux/fb.h>`_."

msgid "验证入口"
msgstr "Validation entry points"

msgid "内核宿主套件由 ``tools/tests/host-suites.list`` 显式登记："
msgstr ""
"Kernel host suites are registered explicitly in ``tools/tests/host-"
"suites.list``:"

msgid ""
"``tools/tests/resource_capacity_runtime_probe.c`` 是原生 Linux ABI 容量探针， "
"``tools/tests/tcp_runtime_probe.c`` 连接测试编排提供的本地 TCP 对端。 二者可用 musl "
"静态构建。完整镜像、私有磁盘和 QEMU 编排归 ReliefOS 持有， 宿主 Linux 上通过只证明参考行为，不能代替 ReliefOS "
"来宾验证。"
msgstr ""
"``tools/tests/resource_capacity_runtime_probe.c`` is a native Linux ABI "
"capacity probe, and ``tools/tests/tcp_runtime_probe.c`` connects to a local "
"TCP peer provided by test orchestration. Both can be statically built with "
"musl. Full images, private disks, and QEMU orchestration belong to ReliefOS;"
" passing on host Linux establishes only reference behavior and cannot "
"replace ReliefOS guest validation."

msgid ""
"``tools/tests/kmodules/memory_layout_probe`` 是独立 Apache-2.0 外部模块， 不要求启用 "
"``MODULE_TESTS``。在使用匹配内核配置及 ABI 的构建环境中， 将其中的 ``Kbuild`` 和 C 文件复制到自有输出目录，再用正式"
" ``make O=<kernel-output> M=<probe-output> modules`` 入口构建；``M`` 目录 "
"会产生构建文件，不能指向源码目录。在来宾使用 ``insmod`` 和 ``rmmod`` 加载、卸载后检查 ``[memory-probe]`` "
"日志：模块只触碰自身取得的 513 页 高于 16 GiB 的连续内存和两页 DMA32 内存，验证零填充及逐页写读， "
"并在所有失败路径释放已取得页面。低内存环境或连续高端内存不足时探针 会报告失败；不能用该失败推断内核其余 RAM 不可用。"
msgstr ""
"``tools/tests/kmodules/memory_layout_probe`` is an independent Apache-2.0 "
"external module that does not require ``MODULE_TESTS``. In a build "
"environment with matching kernel configuration and ABI, copy its ``Kbuild`` "
"and C files into your own output directory, then build through the official "
"``make O=<kernel-output> M=<probe-output> modules`` entry point; the ``M`` "
"directory receives build files and must not point to the source directory. "
"In the guest, load and unload with ``insmod`` and ``rmmod``, then inspect "
"``[memory-probe]`` logs: the module touches only its own 513 contiguous "
"pages above 16 GiB and two DMA32 pages, validates zero filling and per-page "
"writes/reads, and frees acquired pages on every failure path. In low-memory "
"environments or with insufficient contiguous high memory, the probe reports "
"failure; that failure does not imply that the kernel's other RAM is "
"unusable."
